  [ example of Einstein deleted ]

My understanding is that there are two main type of mathematical
imagination.  Some people (like me) think in terms of visual images. 
I don't feel I've understood an equation or concept unless I can
visualise what it means.  Give me images of phase space over an equation
any day.  Other people (particularly linguistically skilled) analyse
maths from a more algebraic 'viewpoint' and they form direct
relationships between symbols.  Euler, I suspect, was one of these. 
